{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And HaShem saw that the wickedness of man was great.</b> Because they sinned through licentiousness, and that desire is great and goes on forever and is never satisfied, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sukkah 52b): 'A small organ in man — when he starves it, it is satisfied.' And likewise they sinned through robbery, and one who loves violence and money is never satisfied with money, but his desire is great and goes on continually. And 'every inclination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil all the day' — this means to say: all the day he is not satisfied by his desire; there is no hour in the day in which he will be sated by it, but every hour he adds to his desire."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:43.168166886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}